    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title"><div><div class="eyebrow">NCAA evidence review · 03 November 2026</div><h1 id="page-title">Forecast quality.<br>Visible limits.</h1><p>Different objectives produce different leaders. Explore the probabilities, point errors and uncertainty behind a separately evaluated college basketball track.</p><div class="league-pill" id="league-label">__TITLE__</div></div><aside class="hero-aside"><strong>One cohort. A clear comparison.</strong><p>Historical results below describe development-exposed research. The current season must build its own record of saved, timestamped forecasts.</p><a href="../__SIBLING__/index.html" class="league-pill">Explore __SIBLING_LABEL__ →</a></aside></section>
    <div class="status-strip"><div><strong>Latest owner attempt stopped before data restoration.</strong><span>0 new real fits · 0 new predictions · 250 invented-fixture tests passed. A later return readback preserved evidence, not scientific credit.</span></div><a href="#current">Read the status ↓</a></div>
    <section class="section" id="historical" aria-labelledby="historical-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Historical evidence</div><h2 id="historical-title">Choose the question first.</h2></div><p>The same pooled selection is shown in each season. A seasonal view changes the evaluation window; it does not choose a new winner.</p></div>
      <div class="filters"><label for="objective">Objective<select id="objective"><option value="probability">Win probability</option><option value="accuracy">Winner accuracy</option><option value="margin">Point margin</option><option value="total">Total points</option></select></label><label for="season">Evaluation window<select id="season"><option value="pooled">Both historical seasons</option><option value="2025">2024–25</option><option value="2026">2025–26</option></select></label><div class="selection-note" id="selection-note"></div></div>
      <div class="metrics" id="metrics" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <div class="chart-grid"><div class="panel"><h3 id="chart-title">Reliability, in ten bins.</h3><p class="subtle" id="chart-subtitle"></p><div id="chart"></div><div class="legend" id="chart-legend"></div><p class="table-note" id="chart-note"></p></div><div class="panel"><h3 id="table-title">Objective-specific selections</h3><p class="subtle">Public IDs preserve the result without exposing private model recipes.</p><div class="data-scroll"><table id="model-table"><caption id="table-caption"></caption><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note" id="table-note"></p></div></div>
      <p class="qualification">The two seasons selected these models after evaluation. They are development-exposed, retrospective comparisons. Historical feature releases use a declared 24-hour assumption; full official-season completeness and prospective performance are not established.</p>
      <div class="panel tradeoff" id="tradeoff"><div><div class="eyebrow">Probability versus accuracy</div><h3>Point estimates tell only part of the story.</h3><p>The probability selection is compared with the accuracy selection on identical games. Whole weeks are resampled within each season, 2,000 times. Intervals describe this exposed selection; they are not adjusted for model search.</p></div><div id="tradeoff-values"></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="current" aria-labelledby="current-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / 2026–27 monitoring</div><h2 id="current-title">A new season needs new evidence.</h2></div><p>The failed attempt never reached its source refresh or evaluation stages. These are gaps in this run, not zero-valued performance scores.</p></div><div class="track-grid"><article class="track"><span class="badge">PRESERVED · NOT REPLACED</span><h3>Original frozen models</h3><p>Parameters, selection and genuine historical forecast timestamps remain unchanged. No new current-season scorecard was produced by this attempt. Reconstructed predictions must remain a separate record.</p><div class="track-footer"><span>New issued rows: <strong>0</strong></span><span>Current metrics: <strong>unavailable</strong></span></div></article><article class="track"><span class="badge">PLANNED · NOT EXECUTED</span><h3>Rolling chronological models</h3><p>Each training origin must exclude unreleased labels and later corrections. New predictions require information available one to two hours before tipoff. More data does not guarantee lower future loss.</p><div class="track-footer"><span>New real fits: <strong>0</strong></span><span>Promotion: <strong>none</strong></span></div></article></div>
      <div class="panel providers"><h3>Three providers. The same qualification standard.</h3><div class="data-scroll"><table><caption>Current-run comparison availability; missing measurements are displayed as unavailable.</caption><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th class="provider-product">Comparable products</th><th>Matched games</th><th>Log loss / ROI</th></tr></thead><tbody id="provider-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="gap-note">Exact event and ordered-team matching, quote clocks, full-game settlement, executable prices and applicable fees are required. No current-season market advantage, hypothetical profit or ROI is established by this attempt.</p></div>
      <details class="source-details"><summary>What failed, and what the later verification proves</summary><p>A stream context manager returned a raw HTTP reader while the caller expected a wrapper-specific iterator. The invented test double returned itself, leaving that integration boundary untested. The first parent-data read failed; return readback then hit the same interface error. A subsequent independent full-byte read verified the saved return. It did not create a completed scientific stage, new fit, forecast or provider comparison.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="engineering" aria-labelledby="engineering-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / Inspect the engineering</div><h2 id="engineering-title">Move a clock. Watch the contract.</h2></div><p>This interaction uses invented inputs only. The executable Python example tests the same classes of failure without credentials, subscriptions or cloud access.</p></div><div class="engineering"><div class="panel"><h3>Information available before 16:00 UTC</h3><p class="subtle">Invented tipoff: 18:00 UTC · decision horizon: two hours.</p><div class="demo-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented contract scenarios"><button type="button" data-scenario="valid" aria-pressed="true">All inputs in time</button><button type="button" data-scenario="late_quote" aria-pressed="false">Late quote</button><button type="button" data-scenario="boundary_label" aria-pressed="false">Boundary label</button><button type="button" data-scenario="settlement" aria-pressed="false">Wrong settlement</button></div><div class="demo-clocks"><div><span>Latest training label</span><strong id="demo-label">15:00 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Quote available</span><strong id="demo-quote">15:55 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Feature available</span><strong>15:10 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Settlement scope</span><strong id="demo-settlement">Full game + overtime</strong></div></div><div class="demo-output" id="demo-output" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="table-note">Passing a comparison contract does not authorize a wager. The public payoff example separately requires explicit price and fee evidence and always emits zero orders.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Reproduce the review mechanism.</h3><p class="subtle">Python 3.11+ · standard library · deterministic invented data.</p><pre class="code">python examples/ncaa_review/contracts.py --demo
python -m unittest discover -s examples/ncaa_review -p 'test_*.py'
python examples/ncaa_review/build_dashboard.py --check</pre><ul class="checklist"><li>Reject future and exact-boundary training labels.</li><li>Pair each provider on the exact same games and products.</li><li>Keep frozen, reconstructed and issued tracks separate.</li><li>Preserve both winning and losing disagreements.</li><li>Verify complete streamed bytes and close the actual reader.</li></ul><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/tree/main/examples/ncaa_review">Read the source, tests and methodology ↗</a></div></div>
    </section>
    <details class="source-details"><summary>Aggregate provenance and public reproducibility boundary</summary><p>The historical objective and season metrics were independently recomputed from authenticated per-game exports. The public report contains aggregates, calibration bins and descriptive uncertainty. It excludes private data, individual forecasts, feature transforms, active model configurations, weights and execution handoffs. The generic invented example is reproducible here; private real-data retraining is not.</p><p>Accepted historical owner-return SHA-256:<br><span class="hash" id="history-hash"></span></p><p>Failed current owner-return SHA-256:<br><span class="hash" id="failed-hash"></span></p><p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/tracks/__LEAGUE__/evidence.json">Inspect the exact public aggregate JSON ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/docs/PUBLICATION_BOUNDARY.md">Publication boundary ↗</a></p></details>
    <p class="print-note">Snapshot: 03 November 2026. Historical research is development-exposed; no prospective market advantage is claimed.</p>
